President Trump says he will respond  forcefully to what he calls the  atrocious use of chemical weapons by  Syria's government the regime is  suspected of attacking the rebel-held  town of Duma outside Damascus with corn  with a chlorine agent more than 40  people reportedly died the president  said a US response is imminent and it  may extend to Syria's allies Iran and  Russia we can't let that happen in our  world we can't let that happen  especially when we're able to because of  the power of the United States because  of the power of our country we're able  to stop it  sat down is traveling in the region  right now he's along the Syria Lebanon  border with Russia's latest response to  the attack good morning we are just a  few miles from the border with Syria  president Trump has called that  suspected chlorine attack barbaric  specifically referencing images of sick  suffocating and dying children and the  president has indicated that all options  including military ones are on the table  the Russian Defense Ministry released  this video which they say shows their  own military's investigation into the  attack and claimed they found no traces  of poisonous substances Moscow has  dismissed allegations of a chemical  attack as fake news following last  year's use of the internationally banned  sarin nerve agent in the Syrian town of  hansha Kuhn the Trump administration  struck Syria with Tomahawk cruise  missiles while Syria has been repeatedly  accused of using chlorine as a weapon it  has not yet prompted a military response  from the Trump administration a strike  from the US would be a new precedent and  could risk escalating tensions with  Syria's allies Iran and Russia whose UN  Ambassador has warned of grave  repercussions if the u.s. launched a  military strike for CBS this morning  I'm Seth Doane in Stora Lebanon
 

